# Apex Grid — AI Coding Rules

You are working with `apex-grid`, a Lit-based web-component data grid by ApexCharts.
Documentation: https://github.com/apexcharts/apexgrid
NPM: apex-grid (with a hyphen — no `apexgrid` package exists)
GitHub: https://github.com/apexcharts/apexgrid
Confirmed versions: apex-grid@5.0.0, lit@^3.3.0 (apex-grid-enterprise@0.10.0 depends on apex-grid ^5.0.0; apexcharts@8.4.1 or later for a `type: 'chart'` column).
Upgrading from 3.x: see "Changed in 4.0" at the end; from 4.x: see "Changed in 4.2 and 5.0".

## Quickstart — register + size the host

The grid styles itself out of the box — there is **no theme CSS to import**.
The one real gotcha is host sizing: it virtualizes rows and needs a bounded
height or it collapses and renders nothing. `setup()` handles both.

### 1. Install
```bash
npm install apex-grid lit
```
That is the whole install: `apex-grid` brings `lit`, `@lit/context` and `@lit-labs/virtualizer`.
There is no theme CSS to import for a styled grid (3.5.0 dropped the old `igniteui-webcomponents`
dependency). An Ignite UI theme never fully themed the grid: 3.x only took its brand and font. From
4.0 the only way to follow an Ignite UI theme is the `apex-grid/ignite-ui` add-on, which needs no extra licence key (not in 3.x;
see "Ignite UI theming" below).

### 2. Register + size — `setup()` does both
```ts
import { setup } from 'apex-grid';
setup();                       // registers <apex-grid> + adopts host sizing. Idempotent.
```
Manual alternative: `import 'apex-grid/define'` (or `ApexGrid.register()`) plus your own
`apex-grid { height: 480px; }`. `setup({ hostStyles: false })` skips the injected sizing.

### 3. Style via `--ag-*` CSS variables (no theme import)
The grid is styled out of the box; retheme by overriding `--ag-*` custom properties on
`apex-grid` or on any ancestor, shadow hosts included (3.6). `configureTheme()` does NOT affect
appearance, and 5.0 removed `setup({ theme })` (it only warned; `setup()` takes `hostStyles` / `tokenStyles`).
The chrome is sized in px since 4.2 and ignores the page's root font size.
```css
apex-grid { height: 480px; --ag-brand: #7c3aed; /* + any --ag-* overrides */ }
```
Dark mode: the `theme="dark"` attribute (`tinted` adds brand chrome; `theme="dark tinted"`).
Since 3.6 a dark grid reads `--ag-dark-*` colour tokens (`--ag-dark-surface`, `--ag-dark-text`, ...)
and IGNORES the light ones (`--ag-surface`, ...), even when set on the dark grid itself.
Brand, sizing and typography tokens are shared. In your own CSS, `var(--ag-brand)` has no
root default: write `var(--ag-brand, #0d6fd3)`.

### Ignite UI theming (new in 4.0)
`import 'apex-grid/ignite-ui';` once (no extra licence key; ES modules only, no script-tag file).
Every grid on the page, shadow roots included, then follows the Ignite UI theme: brand, text,
gridlines, pinned edge, header (`--ig-surface-raised`, 7.5+), state colours, font, enterprise popups.
- Ranking: `--ag-*` you set > family `--apx-*` tokens > Ignite UI > built-in values
  (family-wide: explicit option > product CSS variable > `--apx-*` > named theme/palette > `--ig-*` > defaults).
- Mode: no `theme` attribute follows `--ig-theme-variant` live; `theme="light"`/`"dark"` pins the mode
  (a pinned `light` blocks the dark variant).
- Per grid: `design-system="off"` (`designSystem = false`) drops the Ignite UI colours and font;
  `tokens="off"` (`tokens = false`) drops `--apx-*` and Ignite UI, variant included.
- Live: no `refreshTokens()` needed. With the add-on, the Ignite-following tokens leave the root
  defaults: page CSS reading them needs a fallback, `var(--ag-text, #111827)`.
- New tokens `--ag-overlay`, `--ag-overlay-text` (dark: `--ag-dark-overlay`, `--ag-dark-overlay-text`)
  colour the enterprise popups (apex-grid-enterprise 0.9.0); no default.
- `--ag-font` you set now wins over family and Ignite UI fonts and has no root default: `var(--ag-font, Inter, sans-serif)`.
- BREAKING (4.0): the grid no longer reads `--ig-*` by itself (3.x took the brand and font with no
  import). Without the add-on an Ignite UI stylesheet changes nothing. The 4.0 grid also follows
  `--apx-*` set on `:root`.

### Minimal example

```ts
import { html, render } from 'lit';
import { setup } from 'apex-grid';
import type { ColumnConfiguration } from 'apex-grid';

setup();   // register + host sizing; no theme import needed

type User = { id: number; name: string; age: number; subscribed: boolean };

const data: User[] = [
  { id: 1, name: 'Ada Lovelace',  age: 36, subscribed: true  },
  { id: 2, name: 'Carl Sagan',    age: 62, subscribed: false },
];

// Explicit widths prevent the last-column-stretches trap.
const columns: ColumnConfiguration<User>[] = [
  { key: 'id',         type: 'number',  width: '80px',  sort: true, filter: true },
  { key: 'name',       type: 'string',  width: '240px', sort: true, filter: true },
  { key: 'age',        type: 'number',  width: '100px', sort: true, filter: true },
  { key: 'subscribed', type: 'boolean', width: '140px', sort: true, filter: true },
];

render(
  html`<apex-grid .data=${data} .columns=${columns}></apex-grid>`,
  document.getElementById('app')!,
);
```

### What success looks like

- Visible borders between rows and columns
- Sort arrows (↕) next to each column header
- A filter row below the headers with a "Filter" chip per column
- Hover state on rows
- Smooth scrolling; only ~20 `<apex-grid-row>` in the DOM at any time

---

## Naming

| Form | What it is |
|---|---|
| `apex-grid` | npm package name (with hyphen) |
| `<apex-grid>` | the custom-element tag rendered in the DOM |
| `ApexGrid<T>` | the exported class — used for types and `ApexGrid.register()` |

---

## Critical Rules

1. **Apex Grid is a Lit web component, not a JS class.** Don't `new ApexGrid(...)`. Render `<apex-grid>` and set `.data` / `.columns` as properties.
2. **Two setup steps:** register the element and give the host a bounded height — `setup()` does both. **No theme CSS import is needed** (the grid self-styles via `--ag-*`).
3. **`columns` and `data` are properties, not attributes.** Use property binding.
4. **`column.key` must be a real `keyof T`.** No aliases. Compute derived values in `cellTemplate` from `ctx.data`, the record (4.0); `ctx.row` is the row element, which recycling re-binds to other records.
5. **Set `type` per column.** Primitive `'string'`/`'number'`/`'boolean'` drive sort/filter/editing (default `'string'`). Presentation types also exist: `'select'`, `'rating'`, `'date'`, `'image'`, `'currency'`, `'avatar'`, `'badge'`, `'progress'`, `'sparkline'`, `'chart'` (4.1: an ApexCharts chart per cell; call `setApexCharts(ApexCharts)` once; do not hand-write a `keyed` chart template), `'status'`.
6. **`cellTemplate` and `headerTemplate` must return Lit `TemplateResult`s** (`html\`...\``). Strings render as escaped text.
7. **Sort/filter events fire only for UI-initiated operations.** Programmatic `grid.sort(...)` / `grid.filter(...)` are silent.

---

## Column Configuration

```ts
interface ColumnConfiguration<T, K extends keyof T> {
  key: K;                                        // REQUIRED
  type?: DataType;                               // default 'string' (14 types, see rule 5)
  headerText?: string;                           // default: String(key)
  width?: string;                                // CSS — recommended
  hidden?: boolean;
  resizable?: boolean;
  pinned?: 'start' | 'end' | null;               // freeze during horizontal scroll
  reorderable?: boolean;                         // per-column opt-out of drag reorder
  exportable?: boolean;                          // default true
  editable?: boolean;                            // requires grid editing.enabled
  group?: string;                                // id of a columnGroups spanning header
  validators?: Validator<T, K>[];                // edit-time validation (3.2+)
  sort?:   boolean | { caseSensitive?, comparer? };
  filter?: boolean | { caseSensitive? };
  headerTemplate?: (ctx) => TemplateResult;
  cellTemplate?:   (ctx) => TemplateResult;
  editorTemplate?: (ctx) => TemplateResult;
  // type-specific: options ('select'), max ('rating'/'progress'), format ('date'),
  // shape/alt ('image'), currency/locale ('currency'), badgeVariant, statusVariant, showDelta
}
```

Applied defaults: `{ type: 'string', resizable: false, hidden: false, sort: false, filter: false, exportable: true }`.

### Templates

```ts
import { html } from 'lit';

cellTemplate: ({ value, data, column, row, parent }) =>   // data = the record (4.0)
  html`<strong>${value}</strong> <small>#${data.id}</small>`,
```
Body rows are recycled by default (4.0, `rowRecycling`): a row element can show another record after a
scroll, sort or filter. Read `ctx.data`, never hold `ctx.row` / `ctx.parent` / `grid.rows` across an
`await`, keep no state in template elements (or wrap in `keyed(ctx.data, ...)` from
`lit/directives/keyed.js`), or opt out with `grid.rowRecycling = false` / `row-recycling="false"`.

### Auto-generation — 3-line demo

```ts
render(html`<apex-grid auto-generate .data=${data}></apex-grid>`, root);
// Ignored if `columns` is non-empty. Reset grid.columns = [] before swapping data.
```

---

## Filter Operands

| Type | Operands |
|---|---|
| `'string'` and other non-numeric types | `contains`, `doesNotContain`, `startsWith`, `endsWith`, `equals`, `doesNotEqual`, `empty`, `notEmpty` |
| `'number'`, `'currency'`, `'rating'`, `'progress'` (3.6) | `equals`, `doesNotEqual`, `greaterThan`, `lessThan`, `greaterThanOrEqual`, `lessThanOrEqual`, `empty`, `notEmpty` |
| `'boolean'` | `all`, `true`, `false`, `empty`, `notEmpty` (all unary — no `searchTerm`) |

```ts
import { StringOperands, NumberOperands, BooleanOperands } from 'apex-grid';
grid.filter({ key: 'name', condition: 'contains', searchTerm: 'ad' });
grid.filter({ key: 'subscribed', condition: 'true' });        // unary
grid.filter([
  { key: 'age', condition: 'greaterThan', searchTerm: 30 },
  { key: 'age', condition: 'lessThan',    searchTerm: 50, criteria: 'and' },
]);
```

---

## API

| Property | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `data` | `T[]` | |
| `columns` | `ColumnConfiguration<T>[]` | |
| `autoGenerate` | `boolean` | Ignored if `columns` non-empty |
| `sortConfiguration` | `{ multiple, triState }` | Multi-column + tri-state toggles |
| `dataPipelineConfiguration` | `{ sort?, filter?, quickFilter? } \| undefined` | Server-side hooks; `undefined` until assigned (typed optional in 5.0): assign a whole object, read with `?.` (4.0 removed `pagination`: use `pagination.mode: 'remote'`) |
| `showQuickFilter` / `showExport` / `exportFilename` | `boolean` / `boolean` / `string` | Toolbar search / export menu; `exportFilename` (4.2, default `'data'`) names the menu's download only |
| `selection` / `editing` / `pagination` / `tree` / `expansion` | config objects | Opt-in: `{ enabled, ... }` (see SKILL.md §5) |
| `rowRecycling` (attr `row-recycling`) | `boolean` | Default `true` (4.0); `false` keeps record-keyed rows |
| `showHeader` (attr `show-header`) | `boolean` | Default `true`; `false` (4.0) hides the header rows and filter panel |
| `quickFilter` / `columnReordering` | `string` / `boolean` | Global search / drag-reorder headers |
| `sortExpressions` / `filterExpressions` | array (get/set) | Assigning REPLACES (3.6); `[]` clears. `sort()` / `filter()` add |
| `selectedRows` / `expandedRows` | `T[]` (get/set) | Snapshots; set to replace |
| `rows` (getter) | `ApexGridRow<T>[]` | Currently rendered only (virtualized) |
| `dataView` / `pageItems` (getters) | `readonly T[]` | Full post-filter/sort / current page |
| `totalItems` / `pageCount` (getters) | `number` | With pagination, pinned rows not counted (4.0) |

Feature config additions (4.0): `selection.isRowSelectable: (row) => boolean` (rejected rows get no
checkbox and every selection path skips them, e.g. a pinned total row);
`pagination.paginator: 'full' | 'compact'` (`'compact'`: summary, previous, page / count, next).

| Method | Description |
|---|---|
| `sort(expr \| expr[])` | Programmatic. **No events.** |
| `filter(expr \| expr[])` | Programmatic. **No events.** |
| `clearSort(key?)` / `clearFilter(key?)` | Reset state. |
| `getColumn(keyOrIndex)` / `updateColumns(col \| col[])` | Find / merge columns by `key`. |
| `moveColumn(from, to, position?)` | Reorder within pinning group. |
| `exportToCSV(opts?)` / `exportAs(formatId, opts?)` | Export data (CSV built in). |
| `selectRow`/`deselectRow`/`selectAllRows`/`clearSelection`/`isRowSelected` | Selection. |
| `expandRow`/`collapseRow`/`isRowExpanded` (+ `…TreeRow` variants) | Expansion / tree. |
| `commitEdit()` / `cancelEdit()` | Row-edit batch (`editing.mode: 'row'`). |
| `ApexGrid.register()` | Static; idempotent. |

Events are **UI-initiated only** (programmatic calls are silent). `*-ing` events are
cancellable only with `preventDefault()` (returning `false` cancels nothing, `pageChanging` too); `*-ed` are notifications. Pairs:
`sorting/sorted`, `filtering/filtered`, `quickFilterChanging/Changed`, `pageChanging/Changed`,
`columnPinning/Pinned`, `columnMoving/Moved`, `cellValueChanging/Changed`,
`rowEditStarted/Ended`, `rowSelecting/Selected`, `rowExpanding/Expanded`, `treeRowExpanding/Expanded`.

---

## Server-side data

```ts
grid.dataPipelineConfiguration = {
  filter: async ({ data, grid }) =>
    fetch('/api/users/filter', {
      method: 'POST',
      body: JSON.stringify(grid.filterExpressions),
    }).then((r) => r.json()),
};
```

Built-in pipeline is skipped for whichever operations have a hook. Omit one to keep it in-memory. Hooks fire for both UI and programmatic operations.

---

## Pitfalls — ❌ Wrong vs ✅ Correct

### 1. `new ApexGrid(...)`
❌ `new ApexGrid({ container, columns, data })`
✅ Render `<apex-grid .data=${data} .columns=${columns}></apex-grid>`

### 2. Missing registration
❌ Importing `ApexGrid` without `register()` — `<apex-grid>` is inert.
✅ `import 'apex-grid/define'` once at startup.

### 3. Importing a theme CSS that no longer exists
❌ `import 'igniteui-webcomponents/themes/.../bootstrap.css'` + `configureTheme(...)` — obsolete; no effect.
✅ No import needed for a styled grid; retheme via `--ag-*`. The only required CSS is host height.
To follow an Ignite UI theme, `import 'apex-grid/ignite-ui'` (4.0), not a theme import.

### 4. Stringified attribute
❌ `<apex-grid columns="[...]">`
✅ `.columns=${columns}` / `:columns.prop=` / `[columns]=` / `el.columns = ...`

### 5. `column.key` not a `keyof T`
❌ `{ key: 'fullName' }` when not in `T`
✅ `cellTemplate: ({ data }) => html\`${data.firstName} ${data.lastName}\`` (`data` is the record; `row` is the element)

### 6. String from `cellTemplate`
❌ `cellTemplate: ({ value }) => \`<b>\${value}</b>\``
✅ `cellTemplate: ({ value }) => html\`<b>\${value}</b>\``

### 7. Numbers sorted as strings
❌ `{ key: 'age', sort: true }` (default `type: 'string'`)
✅ `{ key: 'age', type: 'number', sort: true }`

### 8. Faking date columns
❌ `type: 'number'` timestamps or string + custom comparer to handle dates.
✅ `{ key: 'created', type: 'date', format: 'medium' }` — real type; accepts Date/ISO/timestamp.

### 9. Clearing sort/filter
❌ Rebuilding state by hand to clear it.
✅ `grid.clearSort()` / `grid.clearFilter()` (optionally per `key`).

### 10. Expecting events from programmatic calls
❌ `grid.addEventListener('sorted'); grid.sort(...)` — silent.
✅ Wrap the call yourself, or watch `grid.dataView`.

### 11. Wrong package name
❌ `import ... from 'apexgrid'` — no such package.
✅ `import ... from 'apex-grid'`.

### 12. Ignite UI theme without the add-on (4.0)
❌ Ignite UI stylesheet on the page, no `apex-grid/ignite-ui`: `--ig-*` is silently ignored in 4.0.
❌ `theme="light"` on the grid while the page switches to a dark Ignite UI theme: blocks the dark variant.
❌ `import 'apex-grid/ignite-ui'` on apex-grid 3.x: no such module.
✅ apex-grid 4.0, `import 'apex-grid/ignite-ui'` once and leave `theme` unset.

### 13. Treating a row element as a record (4.0)
❌ Reading `ctx.row.data` after an `await`, keeping `grid.rows[i]` as a handle, or an `<input>` / widget in a
`cellTemplate` holding its own state: with recycling the element shows another record after a scroll or sort.
✅ Read `ctx.data`; `keyed(ctx.data, html\`...\`)` for stateful templates; or `grid.rowRecycling = false`.

### 14. Reading the grid role from the host (4.0)
❌ `grid.getAttribute('role')` / `aria-rowcount` on `<apex-grid>`: they moved.
✅ `grid.shadowRoot.querySelector('[part~="table"]')`. An `aria-label` on the host still names the grid.

---

## New in 3.1–3.3

- **Row pinning**: `rowPinning = { enabled }`, `pinRow(row, 'top'|'bottom')`/`unpinRow(row)`, `pinnedRows` getter, `rowPinning`/`rowPinned` events.
- **Row reordering**: `rowReordering = { enabled, applyToData?, handle? }`, `moveRow(from, to, position?)`, `rowMoving`/`rowMoved` events (clears on sort).
- **Inline-edit undo/redo**: `editing.history = { enabled, stackSize? }`, `undo()`/`redo()`/`clearHistory()`, `canUndo`/`canRedo`, `historyChanged` event.
- **Validators**: `column.validators: Validator[]` + `required`/`min`/`max`/`pattern`/`custom` factories, `cellValidationFailed` event.
- **Column groups**: `columnGroups = [{ id, headerText }]` + `column.group` (members contiguous within a pin region).
- **State/schema**: `getState()`/`setState()`/`getSchema()`, `rowId`, `stateChanged` event (`setState` is partial + defensive).
- **Programmatic (these DO emit events, unlike sort/filter)**: `gotoPage`/`nextPage`/`setPageSize`/…, `setQuickFilter()`, `pinColumn`/`unpinColumn`.
- **Localization**: `localeText` (`GridLocaleText`), `localize()`, `esLocale` export.
- **Misc**: `columnMenu`/`columnSeparator`; `exportToCSV`/`exportAs` `source: 'view'|'page'|'selected'|'all'`.
- Full detail: `references/state-and-features.md`.

---

## Changed in 3.6

- `sortExpressions` / `filterExpressions` assignment REPLACES the sort / filter (`[]` or `null` clears).
  Assigning one expression at a time keeps only the last: assign the full list, or `grid.sort(expr)` to add.
- `sorted`, `filtered`, `pageChanged`, `quickFilterChanged` fire after the pipeline run, so `dataView` is fresh
  in the listener, async hooks included.
- `currency`, `rating`, `progress` columns filter with the number operands; a `contains` on them is dropped.
- A sort `comparer` receives raw values (original casing, `null` included); empty cells sort last otherwise.
- `applyEdits([{ row, column, value }])` names a row by record (any page, pinned); `rowIndex` stays page-relative.
- `grid.ownsEvent(e)`: events bubble, so filter out a nested master-detail grid's events with it.
- `expansion.exportParts` re-exports parts used in `detailTemplate`; every row part now works with `apex-grid::part()`.
- `rowMoving` / `rowMoved` add `position` and `toIndex`; a row move on a sorted grid clears the sort.
- Row edit mode: validators get the staged row as `ctx.data`; checkbox and `ctx.commit` join the row edit.
- Replacing `grid.data` with new records clears undo history; `grid.data = null` shows an empty grid.
- CSV export prefixes formula-like text with `'` (`exportToCSV({ escapeFormulas: false })` to opt out);
  booleans export `true` only for `true`; currency / progress export as numbers.

---

## Changed in 4.0 (upgrading from 3.x)

Breaking:
- Body rows are recycled by default (`rowRecycling`): read `ctx.data` in templates, or set
  `rowRecycling = false` / `row-recycling="false"` for record-keyed rows.
- `role` (`grid` / `treegrid`), `aria-rowcount`, `aria-colcount`, `aria-multiselectable` and the
  accessible name moved from the host to the inner `[part~="table"]` element.
- An Ignite UI theme does nothing until `import 'apex-grid/ignite-ui'`; `--ag-font` has no root default.
- Pagination: pinned rows no longer count toward `totalItems` / pages; a local page change no longer runs
  custom sort / filter hooks; `DataPipelineConfiguration.pagination` and `DataPipelineParams.type`
  `'pagination'` are removed (types only; the hook was never called).
- `min()` / `max()` fail a value that is not a number (3.x passed `'abc'`).
- Types / DOM: `ctx.data` is required in the cell context; `ApexGridPaginator.pageSizeOptions` is
  `readonly number[]`; the paginator's previous button id is `prev`; protected
  `ApexGrid.headerRowCount` and `ApexGridHeaderRow.renderDragGhost` removed.

New:
- `showHeader` (`show-header="false"`), `selection.isRowSelectable`, `pagination.paginator: 'compact'`.
- `apex-grid::part()` for every paginator part (`paginator`, `paginator-size`, `paginator-info`,
  `paginator-controls`, `paginator-page`, `paginator-button`, `paginator-first` / `-prev` / `-next` /
  `-last`) and toolbar part (`toolbar`, `toolbar-search`, `search-field`, `search-icon`, `search-input`,
  `toolbar-actions`, `toolbar-action`, `export`, `export-trigger`, `export-menu`, `export-menu-item`, ...).
- `ctx.data` in cell and editor templates; a cell template's `ctx.commit` writes to it.
- IME input in the cell editor, filter panel and quick filter; the filter panel and `min()` / `max()` read
  full-width digits and the column `locale`'s grouping (`1.234,5` under `de-DE`) and currency marks.
- Locale keys: `toolbar.exportCsv`, `filter.and` / `filter.or`, `cell.rating`, `cell.true` / `cell.false`,
  `validation.required` / `.min` / `.max` / `.pattern`; `ValidatorContext.localize(key, params?)`.
- Ignite UI add-on (`apex-grid/ignite-ui`) and the family `--apx-*` tokens.

---

## Changed in 4.2 and 5.0 (upgrading from 4.x)

5.0 removes what 4.2 deprecated; an app using none of these names upgrades without edits:
- Toolbar `placeholder` / `debounce`, paginator `pageSizeLabel` (`page-size-label`): removed. Use
  `localeText` keys `'toolbar.searchPlaceholder'` and `'pagination.rowsPerPage'`. The quick filter waits 200 ms.
- Locale keys `filter.filter`, `chart.placeholder`, `ai.answer`, `formula.error.*`: removed (never rendered);
  delete them from typed `localeText` objects.
- `setup({ theme })` / `ApexGridSetupOptions.theme`: removed (it only warned).
- `grid.dataPipelineConfiguration` is typed optional (`undefined` until assigned): read with `?.`.

New in 4.2:
- `exportFilename` (attr `export-filename`, default `'data'`) names the toolbar export menu's file;
  `exportToCSV()` without `filename` still downloads `data.csv`, and an explicit `filename` wins.
- Type exports: `BadgeVariant`, `StatusVariant`, `ColumnDateFormat`, `ColumnSelectOption`, `ToolbarAction`.
- Chrome (toolbar, paginator, header actions, filter row, menus, toggles) sized in px, not by the root font size.
- Locale keys (enterprise panels): `panel.backToGrid`, `panel.shortcutHint`, `chart.title`, `chart.series.*`,
  `formula.parse.*`.
- Wide grids: rows are virtualized, columns are not; with hundreds of columns hide the unneeded ones.

---

## Dev-server reminder

ES module imports require an HTTP server — opening with `file://` fails CORS. Use Vite (`npm create vite@latest`) or any static server.
